# Frontend Rules

## Stack

- Next.js 14 (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, vega-embed v5
- Package manager: `npm`
- All components are in `frontend/src/components/`
- Shared utilities in `frontend/src/lib/`

## Component Map (current)

| File | Role | Touch? |
|------|------|--------|
| `page.tsx` | Shell — all state + WS routing | ✅ Yes (add features here) |
| `TopBar.tsx` | Logo + connection pill | Only for UI changes |
| `LeftPanel.tsx` | Query input + log + history | Only for UI changes |
| `LogStream.tsx` | Activity log rows + blink cursor | Only for log behavior |
| `RightPanel.tsx` | Vega chart + SQL panel | Only for result display |
| `VegaChart.tsx` | vega-embed lifecycle | ⛔ Keep unchanged |
| `lib/ws.ts` | WebSocket class | ⛔ Keep unchanged |

## Color Tokens (globals.css)

All colors are CSS variables — never hardcode hex values in components.

```
--bg            #070b10   Main background
--bg-panel      #0d1117   Sidebar / header panels
--bg-input      #161b22   Input fields
--bg-log        #0a0e14   Log box background
--border        #30363d   Standard borders
--border-subtle #21262d   Subtle dividers
--text-primary  #e6edf3   Primary text
--text-secondary #8b949e  Secondary text
--text-muted    #484f58   Muted / labels
--accent        #06b6d4   Teal — buttons, active borders, icons
--accent-deep   #0891b2   Gradient endpoint
--accent-glow   #06b6d422 Focus ring
--accent-dim    #06b6d444 History active border
--accent-hist   #071922   History active background
--green         #3fb950   Success / connected
--green-bg      #0d2b14   Connected pill background
--green-border  #238636   Connected pill border
--kw-color      #06b6d4   SQL keywords (.kw)
--fn-color      #a5f3fc   SQL functions (.fn)
--id-color      #67e8f9   SQL identifiers (.id)
--lit-color     #cffafe   SQL literals (.lit)
```

## State Shape (page.tsx)

```typescript
query: string              // textarea value
logs: LogEntry[]           // current query's activity log
history: HistoryItem[]     // past queries, prepended on submit
vegaSpec: string | null    // Vega-Lite JSON string from backend
sql: string                // generated SQL
sqlVisible: boolean        // SQL panel open/closed
isLoading: boolean         // disables submit while running
connected: boolean         // true after WS auth resolves
resultTitle: string        // current result heading (= submitted query)
```

## WS Event Routing (page.tsx)

The event handler in `useEffect` routes backend messages to state:

| Event type | Action |
|------------|--------|
| `progress` | Mark any active log entry done; append `{icon:"run", active:true}` |
| `sql` | Append `{icon:"sql", active:false, text: sql.slice(0,40)+"…"}`; setSql |
| `result` | Mark any active done; setVegaSpec; setSql; setIsLoading(false) |
| `error` | Mark any active done; append error entry; setIsLoading(false) |

Important: the mark-done logic flips **any** entry where `e.active === true`, NOT just the last entry by index. This is correct because a `sql` event (active:false) can appear between two `progress` events.

## LogEntry Type

```typescript
type LogEntry = {
  time: string;
  icon: "done" | "run" | "sql";
  text: string;
  active?: boolean;
}
```

- `done` → ✓ green — completed step
- `run`  → ⏳ accent — in-progress step (or error)
- `sql`  → ⬡ accent — SQL display line (never flips to done)

## Adding a New Left Panel Section

LeftPanel has three sections separated by `var(--border-subtle)`. To add a fourth:

1. Add a new `<div>` with `padding: "12px 16px"` and `borderBottom: "1px solid var(--border-subtle)"`
2. Add the section label with the uppercase style pattern already used by "Activity" / "History"
3. Pass new data via props from `page.tsx`

## SQL Syntax Highlighting (RightPanel.tsx)

`highlightSQL()` applies CSS classes via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. The replacement order matters:

1. Identifiers first (backtick/double-quoted) → `.id` — prevents matching class names in later spans
2. String literals → `.lit`
3. Numbers → `.lit`
4. Functions → `.fn`
5. Keywords → `.kw`

`SUM/COUNT/AVG/MIN/MAX` are **not** in the keywords regex — they're in functions only (prevents double-wrapping).

## Client Components

Any component using hooks or browser APIs needs `"use client"` at the top:

```tsx
"use client";
import { useState, useEffect } from "react";
```

`page.tsx`, `LeftPanel.tsx`, `LogStream.tsx`, `RightPanel.tsx`, `TopBar.tsx` all have this.
`VegaChart.tsx` has this.

## Env Vars

```
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_KEY    Your DataLens user key (from POST /api/register)
NEXT_PUBLIC_DSN        Postgres connection string
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL     WebSocket URL (default: ws://localhost:8000/ws/query)
```

`NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix is required for browser-side access in Next.js.

## What NOT to Do

- Never pass `null` to `VegaChart` — its prop is `spec: string`. Guard with `vegaSpec ?`
- Never call `view.finalize()` manually — `VegaChart` manages its own lifecycle
- Never add features to `ws.ts` — it's intentionally minimal
- Never add `onclose` reconnect logic to `ws.ts` without a plan (see spec: out of scope for v1)
- Never use `key={i}` on lists that could be reordered (index keys are OK on append-only logs)
- Never import from `@/components/QueryInput` — it was deleted (absorbed into LeftPanel)
